    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"Round 1 only measured the knapsack grid iso_3.15. All four proposals from last round were refused because their rationales quoted a rounded whole-recipe KL value. This round's rationales quote only exact values from the cited records. The budget is 403/128 bits per weight and iso_3.15 already sits just below it. A swap between equal-size layers is budget-neutral only when the downgraded layer is cheap to downgrade. All the int3→int2 KL costs on record are large, so there is no measured cheap downgrade to pay for upgrades. That leaves two paths. First, option changes that keep the bits the same: act_order and damp in the GPTQ family. Second, freeing bits by setting a coarser group_size on the many rht_gptq_int3 layers and spending them on the MLP layers where the most loss concentrates: 14.down, 27.gate, 3.up and 1.up.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"iso_actorder\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"No change in bits. The loss sits in low-bit GPTQ MLP layers, for example 27.up gptq_int3 at 0.0057182 [Ef04d8aa7bded], whose activation kurtosis is 1090.09 [E24beed188b6a]. act_order=true quantizes the high-activation columns first, so it should cut error for these outlier-heavy inputs. This is a measurement of base iso_3.15 [E514ab09c524e] with act_order=true on every GPTQ method.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"Ef04d8aa7bded\",\"E24beed188b6a\"]},{\"name\":\"iso_damp_high\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05}},\"rationale\":\"No change in bits. The single-layer table [E1c9e17401f6f] and the profiles [E24beed188b6a] were calibrated on short windows. Raising damp=0.05 regularizes the Hessian against overfitting to the calibration set, which should help on the validation windows of base iso_3.15 [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E1c9e17401f6f\",\"E24beed188b6a\"]},{\"name\":\"rht3_g256_mlp_upgrades\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[{\"block\":14,\"kind\":\"down_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":27,\"kind\":\"gate_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int4\"},{\"block\":3,\"kind\":\"up_proj\",\"method\":\"gptq_int4\"}],\"options\":{\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight.group_size\":256}},\"rationale\":\"Setting group_size=256 on rht_gptq_int3 halves its scale overhead. The freed bits pay for three MLP upgrades. 14.down goes from rht_gptq_int2 at 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065] to rht_gptq_int3 at 0.00181478 [E90bd4b2f3645]. 27.gate goes from rht_gptq_int3 at 0.00498703 [Efa0bb391da67] to rht_gptq_int4 at 0.00153131 [Ef428ac081334]. 3.up goes from rht_gptq_int3 at 0.0064177 [E6f4f7ea296d5] to gptq_int4 at 0.00237732 [Ef4ee8cb4969e]. Base is iso_3.15 [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\",\"E90bd4b2f3645\",\"Efa0bb391da67\",\"Ef428ac081334\",\"E6f4f7ea296d5\",\"Ef4ee8cb4969e\"]}]}",
